From e486633ae39877f402aba5521cebd5b6f97ab249 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5kjn1: support Piano factory 19.2 MHz modes

Use the exact Qtech Piano register order for 4080x3060 and 4080x2296 at
30 fps, 3840x2160 at 60 fps and 8160x6120 at 10.05 fps. The existing
24 MHz mode tables remain available for boards using that input clock.

The factory table uses a 19.2 MHz input, a 857.6 MHz CSI link and a
separate VT PLL for exposure and frame timing. Report the VT pixel rate
through the standard control instead of using CSI transport bandwidth.

Source: same-device static ODM sensor module configuration,
com.qti.sensormodule.piano_qtech_s5kjn1sq03_wide_i.bin
SHA256: 43567b617138acdb373f63e49c953aa5df64d421de5f721098a03e8ec23a1140
